linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postinst: verify that /boot/efi is a vfat ESP with PARTLABEL=esp before
    writing anything. This prevents a misconfigured fstab from making the
    package overwrite an unrelated filesystem.
  * postinst: fail an upgrade before replacing the kernel/DTB when the ESP
    has no extlinux.conf, instead of warning and configuring a kernel that
    the boot chain cannot reach. Existing boot entries are still preserved.

