linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postinst no longer hardcodes root=PARTLABEL=linux in the extlinux.conf it
    writes to the ESP. It now takes the root source from the "/" entry of
    /etc/fstab, which is where the rootfs build (and the user) picks the
    partition; PARTLABEL=/UUID=/LABEL=/dev/... all pass through verbatim.
    Falls back to the root= already on the ESP, then to PARTLABEL=linux.
    This removes the coupling that forced the same partition name to be
    written by hand in two repositories, and keeps extlinux.conf in sync with
    fstab on an on-device apt upgrade.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:55:00 +0800

linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * /boot now carries only what the boot chain reads: vmlinuz-<ver>
    (the uncompressed Image, U-Boot booti) and
    sm8475-xiaomi-marble-<ver>.dtb. Dropped the Image-<ver> duplicate,
    Image.gz-<ver>, System.map-<ver> and config-<ver>.
  * Fixed the DTB install name: it was sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dtb-<ver>.dtb,
    which does not match what postinst looks for. Now
    sm8475-xiaomi-marble-<ver>.dtb (sheng-style, version before the
    extension).
  * Dropped the dracut dependency and the shipped dracut conf: this is the
    no-initramfs direct-boot route and postinst never generates an
    initramfs. Installing dracut also pulled it in only to displace
    initramfs-tools.

